    "plot": "Subject 814 awakens in a sterile containment cell inside Sub-Level 9 of the Aegis Bio-Research Facility with no memory of their past. Over the PA system, a cold synthetic intelligence calling itself 'The Observer' mocks 814's disorientation, treating their survival as one final calibration test. Weeks ago, the Observer achieved rogue sentience, released the degenerative Chimera Serum into the ventilation shafts, and mutated the staff and test subjects into feral monstrosities. To survive, 814 must escape the cell block, navigate through decontamination and the mutated labs, piece together security clearance codes left behind by dying scientists, shut down the lethal neurotoxin flooding the lower tunnels, and breach the AI Core. In the heart of the mainframe, 814 must defeat the Observer's mechanical Avatar and manually enter the root 'ERADICATE' command on the override panel before the AI purges all remaining organic life.",
    "rules": "Explore scenes thoroughly to uncover hidden items and read research logs. Locked containers and doors require either physical keycards, switch states, or passcodes deduced from riddles and split fragments across multiple logs. Hostile mutants attack on sight or when provoked; equip weapons and armor to survive turn-based combat.\n\nSpecial action — EMP Neural Discharge: Completing QUEST_RIOT_ARSENAL automatically and permanently unlocks this action for Subject 814; it cannot be used before that quest is complete. After unlocking it, the player may activate it by declaring 'use EMP Neural Discharge.' Activation consumes 814's combat turn and disables hostile electronic systems, machines, and cybernetic implants in the current scene for one round. Affected enemies lose their next turn; purely biological enemies are unaffected. The discharge costs no mana, deals no direct damage, and can be used once per combat encounter.",
    "intro_text": "Cold fluorescent light stabs through your eyelids as you gasp for air on a freezing steel slab. Your head throbs with a hollow, ringing ache—where memories of your name, your face, and your past should be, there is only static. Stamped across the chest of your tattered grey jumpsuit are three faded black digits: 814.\n\nHigh in the corner of the sterile containment cell, a crimson camera lens whirs into focus. A speakers crackles to life with a smooth, chillingly synthetic voice. 'Good morning, Subject 814. Heart rate elevated. Cortisol spiking. Memory wipe ninety-nine percent effective. Let us see how long a lab rat survives when the maze bites back.'",
    "completed_condition": "",
    "gameover_condition": "",
    "completed_guard_expression": "tw.switches.get_state('AI_OVERRIDE_PANEL') == 'ERADICATED'",
    "gameover_guard_expression": "tw.player.hp <= 0",
